From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:25:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: crtc: Let DRM manage the CRTC

sun4i_drv no longer calls drm_mode_config_cleanup() itself (drm/sun4i:
drv: Do not call drm_mode_config_cleanup()). The managed release of
drm_mode_config_init() destroys the mode objects at the last
drm_dev_put() instead, after component_unbind_all(), and, while
userspace still holds the device open, after the display engine device
has released its devres.

The CRTC lives in devm memory of the display engine device and is
destroyed through its .destroy hook, so it is cleaned up on freed
memory in that case.

Allocate it with drmm_kzalloc() and initialise it with
drmm_crtc_init_with_planes(). The managed action calls
drm_crtc_cleanup() before the memory is freed. The managed variant
wants a NULL .destroy, so drop the hook.

Not covered: the planes of the CRTC, converted separately.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: the DisplayPort device unbound and bound
again three times with a monitor attached, without an oops; the picture
returns after each bind.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_crtc.c | 14 +++++++-------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_crtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_crtc.c
index 55312a0115ce..8219ccb710cd 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_crtc.c
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 #include <drm/drm_atomic.h>
 #include <drm/drm_atomic_helper.h>
 #include <drm/drm_crtc.h>
+#include <drm/drm_managed.h>
 #include <drm/drm_modes.h>
 #include <drm/drm_print.h>
 #include <drm/drm_probe_helper.h>
@@ -258,7 +259,6 @@ static int sun4i_crtc_verify_crc_source(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 static const struct drm_crtc_funcs sun4i_crtc_funcs = {
 	.atomic_destroy_state	= drm_atomic_helper_crtc_destroy_state,
 	.atomic_duplicate_state	= drm_atomic_helper_crtc_duplicate_state,
-	.destroy		= drm_crtc_cleanup,
 	.page_flip		= drm_atomic_helper_page_flip,
 	.reset			= drm_atomic_helper_crtc_reset,
 	.set_config		= drm_atomic_helper_set_config,
@@ -279,7 +279,7 @@ struct sun4i_crtc *sun4i_crtc_init(struct drm_device *drm,
 	struct drm_plane *primary = NULL, *cursor = NULL;
 	int ret, i;
 
-	scrtc = devm_kzalloc(drm->dev, sizeof(*scrtc), GFP_KERNEL);
+	scrtc = drmm_kzalloc(drm, sizeof(*scrtc), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!scrtc)
 		return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
 	scrtc->engine = engine;
@@ -308,11 +308,11 @@ struct sun4i_crtc *sun4i_crtc_init(struct drm_device *drm,
 		}
 	}
 
-	ret = drm_crtc_init_with_planes(drm, &scrtc->crtc,
-					primary,
-					cursor,
-					&sun4i_crtc_funcs,
-					NULL);
+	ret = drmm_crtc_init_with_planes(drm, &scrtc->crtc,
+					 primary,
+					 cursor,
+					 &sun4i_crtc_funcs,
+					 NULL);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(drm->dev, "Couldn't init DRM CRTC\n");
 		return ERR_PTR(ret);
